mintcam (0.5.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * Fix the photo button, whose text was invisible. The footer had a
    stylesheet with bare declarations, and a background-color set that way
    propagates to the child widgets and overrides the #primary rule: the button
    kept a dark background while the text colour stayed dark, so "Scatta foto"
    was drawn on a dark background. Every container stylesheet in the window is
    now scoped to the widget it belongs to (QWidget#footer and friends), which
    is what Qt expects.
  * Fix the recording, which played back faster than it was recorded. The
    recorder was written once per preview timer tick, so with an fps setting the
    camera cannot reach (the default is 88) the same frame was written several
    times and the video ran at about three times the real speed. Only new
    frames are written now, and the declared frame rate is the one measured on
    the camera instead of the requested one.
  * Tell the difference between "no webcam" and "webcam busy". When another
    application holds the camera the message used to say that no webcam was
    detected, which is wrong and misleading: the camera was there and the user
    was told the opposite.
  * The face auto-framing now reports when the classifier cannot be loaded
    instead of staying silent, and disables itself like the other failure
    paths.
  * Bring back the share and streaming buttons in the footer, which had been
    dropped. Sharing copies the photo to the clipboard or opens the folder for
    a video: no web page is opened pretending to share, and nothing is uploaded.

 -- Alex Mirici <hilliedmikerano@gmail.com>  Tue, 13 Oct 2026 01:10:00 +0200

